# Shell scripts must be checked out with LF, whatever the platform.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF in the working tree and is supposed to rewrite it back on the way into a commit.
# It does not always: scan-tells.sh was staged with CRLF on all 160 lines, which Git Bash
# tolerates and every real Linux shell does not. The failure is
# `$'\r': command not found` on line 2 and a syntax error a few lines later, and it only
# ever appears for somebody else, on a machine the author does not have.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The generated assets. Marked binary so no end-of-line conversion is ever applied to
# them: a PNG or a woff2 with two bytes rewritten is a corrupt file, not a diff.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary

# SVG is text and benefits from real diffs, but it is generated here, so it is checked out
# with LF to keep the bytes identical to what the generator wrote.
*.svg text eol=lf
